| heuristic--heart-rate-work-capacity-tests-for-lifters | FIX | Novik protocol (PDF 340) and PWC-170 protocol and formula (PDF 341) checked; all 11 Table 6.5 rows match the image. Overreach: the entry lists "pulls 0%" as part of the table's inconsistency with "+70%". The text applies the 70% only "in each case **where there is significant eccentric action**" (PDF 341), so 0% for the clean and snatch pulls fits that qualifier. The real inconsistencies are the ratios above or between: bench +100%, squat clean about +88%, split clean +40%, split snatch about +33%, good morning about +49%, jerk about +11%, power clean about +6%. | Reword to: "...the table's ratios differ: back squat about +71% and half squat about +68% fit, but bench press +100% and squat clean about +88% exceed it, and split clean, split snatch, good morning, jerk and power clean (about +6% to +49%) fall between; the pulls at 0% fit the 'significant eccentric action' qualifier." |
