## Counts

GO 22, FIX 6, NO-GO 0.

## Overall verdict: GO AFTER FIXES

Required fixes:
1. early-history: "on the next page" becomes "on the same page" (PDF 325).
2. progress-skills: "third bullet" becomes "second bullet" (PDF 329).
3. volume-intensity calculation: the worked example keeps an 80 kg set (66.7% of 1RM), so it does not follow the 70% rule; reword (PDF 334).
4. cybernetic periodisation: soften the Siff attribution; the page names neither author (PDF 339-340, 345).
5. heart-rate tests: reword the Table 6.5 inconsistency; the pulls at 0% fit the "significant eccentric action" qualifier (PDF 341).
6. periodisation controversy: separate the Horwill and Tschiene citations from the British-decline claim and add Tschiene's actual point (PDF 344).
